   "text": {
    "L1": "A construction uses only a compass and an unmarked ruler. It does not use a protractor.",
    "L2": "Here is how to construct 30° at O on ray OA.",
    "L3": "First, draw an arc with centre O, cutting the ray at P. With centre P and the same width, cut that arc at Q.",
    "L4": "Join O to Q. The triangle is equilateral, so angle POQ is 60°.",
    "L5": "Now use equal arcs from P and Q to cross at R. Join O to R to bisect the 60° angle.",
    "L6": "The new angle is 30°. Equal radii and crossing arcs make the construction exact in principle.",
    "L7": "Remember: construct 60°, then bisect it for 30°. Which angle did we construct?"
   },
